# Virtual providers, pinned here so the build is non-interactive.
#
# These have to be listed at THIS level, not in a metapackage's depends=().
# A provider reached through a metapackage still prompts: the Plasma build
# listed cronie via shani-tools-extra and pacman still asked "2 providers
# available for cron", because only a package named on the pacstrap command
# line counts as a chosen provider. --noconfirm does not help either; it
# answers install confirmations, not provider selection, so with no tty the
# prompt reads EOF and silently takes the default.
#
# iptables   provides libxtables.so, which iproute2 depends on, which `base`
#            depends on -- so the prompt is unavoidable without this line.
# crun       provides oci-runtime, wanted by podman and buildah (shani-core).
# exim       provides smtp-forwarder, wanted by arpwatch
#            (shani-tools-network). It is also what cronie's smtp-server
#            resolves to, so this covers both.
iptables
crun
exim
